<title>NEW ZEALAND: Only Telecom of NZ ADRs respond to soaring Dow.</title>
<headline>Only Telecom of NZ ADRs respond to soaring Dow.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apart from Telecom, New Zealand ADRs weaker or flat in afternoon New York trade despite the Dow's 80.43 surge to 6740 at 7.35 a.m. NZT.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$31 1/2	  nil   *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$28 5/8	 -0 1/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 5/8	  nil   *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$15	     -0 1/8 *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$82	     +0 1/2 *</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  33 1/2		nil</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  untraded</p>
<p>Thistle	  London  191		 +5</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  241 1/2	   +2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  150 1/2	   +1</p>
<p>Templeton	London  146 1/2	   +3</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.26	    +5</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.59	    -2</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$2.60	    +4</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
